Which TCP field is used to ensure ordered data delivery?
a: Sequence Number
In TCP congestion control, what happens during the slow-start phase?
 a: The congestion window increases exponentially.
How does TCP ensure reliability in data transmission?
 a: By using checksums and acknowledgments.
Why does the TIME-WAIT state exist during TCP connection termination?
 a: To ensure all delayed packets are received.
Which TCP congestion control algorithm reduces the window size when congestion is detected?
 b: Additive Increase, Multiplicative Decrease (AIMD)
What happens when a TCP sender detects packet loss?
 a: It reduces the congestion window size.
Why is TCP considered connection-oriented?
 b: It ensures data is delivered in sequence and without errors.
Purpose of the three-way handshake?
 b: To establish a reliable connection before data transfer.
Which TCP mechanism controls the flow of data to prevent overwhelming the receiver?
 c: Sliding Window
Main difference between Go-Back-N and Selective Repeat?
 a: Go-Back-N retransmits all packets after a loss, while Selective Repeat only retransmits lost packets.
